# Cr - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * Cr.ugur.ang Cr
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -110 meV (4.33 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against neutron dispersion the hard sets average 9.5 % over the 29 elements that have one, against 12.7 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 23 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: SUSPECT.  At 600 K this runs at 556 K where equipartition gives 300; something is releasing energy.  Check before trusting it.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Cr at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Cr Cr Cr 8.3398107025044261 0.28298307754667212 0.27546898798807218 3.7462958742310821 0.051502009764652579 -0.36201274440217235 0.013773677924408341 7.4981400000000002 3.7462959929609139 -1 1.6655974807387905 -0.30664727724332752
